# ── 24klabs.ai response headers ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Cache values follow Cloudflare's own ops manual §6
# (skills/cloudflare/references/cf-ops-manual-2026-08-28.md on the bus).
#
# s-maxage is the number that matters here. It controls the EDGE cache, and the
# audience is machines — probers and crawlers ignore max-age entirely.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE ADDING A BLANKET /* CACHE RULE.
# The manual's example opens with `/*  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600,
# s-maxage=7200`. Do not copy that here. This site serves a PAID endpoint:
# /api/v1/verify is x402-gated at $2.00 and fails closed without a payment
# signature. Caching it hands the product out for free, with no error and no log
# — the same hazard CACHE_DECISION_2026-08-28.md found for api.24klabs.ai, except
# that doc only names the subdomain and this one is on the Pages site itself.
# So: nothing is cached by default. Caching is granted per path, deliberately.
#
# AND THE HEADERS BELOW ARE NOT ENOUGH ON THEIR OWN. A Cache Rule set to
# "Ignore cache-control header and use this TTL" overrides everything here,
# including the no-store. The dashboard rule MUST exclude /api/* explicitly.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; connect-src 'self' raw.githubusercontent.com; img-src 'self' data: https:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline';
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()

# ── never cached ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# /api/v1/verify  — paid, $2.00, must revalidate payment on every single request
# /api/probe      — a live knock; a cached liveness result is a false verdict
/api/*
  Cache-Control: no-store, no-cache, must-revalidate
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex

# ── the machine-readable catalog ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Free and public by doctrine. The heaviest-hit path we can safely serve cold.
/directory.json
  Content-Type: application/json
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, s-maxage=7200
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *

# ── the shelf ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 501 prerendered listing pages. Rebuilt by the Directory Wire; the edge cache
# does NOT purge on deploy, so a merged entry appears after the TTL expires, not
# at deploy. 2h is the Free-plan floor and the wire runs daily — acceptable.
/listing/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, s-maxage=7200

/directory/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, s-maxage=7200

# ── agent-facing static ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/llms.txt
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, s-maxage=7200
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
